11
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Surf's Up is a 2007 American animated mockumentary sports comedy film directed by Ash Brannon
and Chris Buck, and written by Brannon, Buck, Don Rhymer and Chris Jenkins.

12
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
Produced by Sony Pictures Animation, the film features the voices of Shia
LaBeouf, Jeff Bridges, Zooey Deschanel, Jon Heder, and James Woods.

13
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:19,636
It is a parody of surfing documentaries, such as The Endless Summer and
Riding Giants, with parts of the plot parodying North Shore.

14
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:11,454
Real-life surfers Kelly Slater and Rob Machado have
vignettes as their penguin surfer counterparts.

15
00:57:57,272 --> 00:58:03,272
To obtain the desired hand-held documentary feel, the film's animation
team motion-captured a physical camera operator's moves.

16
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
Surf's Up was released in the United States on June 8, 2007, by Sony Pictures Releasing, and received generally
positive reviews from critics, with praise for the animation, humor and unique mockumentary setup.

17
01:05:40,909 --> 01:05:46,909
The film grossed $152 million against a budget of $100 million, and was
nominated for Best Animated Feature at the 80th Academy Awards.

18
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
A sequel, Surf's Up 2: WaveMania, was released in 2017.

19
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
A TV series is in development at Atomic Cartoons.

20
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The film explores themes of sea, surfer, surfboard, wave, world cup.

21
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
The tone is lighthearted.
